WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:04.880
It takes a lot of work for an actor to convincingly
play a character.

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:09.980
It's remarkable, then, when they agree to
take on more than one part in a film.

00:00:09.990 --> 00:00:16.020
Even more remarkable: These stars were somehow
able to keep their extra roles and cameos

00:00:16.020 --> 00:00:18.380
a secret… for awhile, at least.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:22.760
Warwick Davis is an icon of science fiction
and fantasy films.

00:00:22.760 --> 00:00:27.940
Apart from his starring role in Willow, he's
played four different characters in four different

00:00:27.940 --> 00:00:32.380
Star Wars movies, his most famous being Wicket
in Return of the Jedi.

00:00:32.560 --> 00:00:38.900
He also had multiple roles in another beloved
fantasy film franchise: the Harry Potter movies.

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:44.840
In seven out of the eight movies, Davis appears
as Professor Filius Flitwick, professor of

00:00:44.840 --> 00:00:47.460
Charms and head of Ravenclaw House.

00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:55.540
"One of a wizard's most rudimentary skills
is levitation, or the ability to make objects

00:00:55.540 --> 00:00:56.160
fly."

00:00:56.900 --> 00:01:01.970
His appearance is obscured only a little,
with some glasses and a huge mustache.

00:01:01.970 --> 00:01:05.340
Throughout the series, however, he put in
additional appearances.

00:01:05.340 --> 00:01:09.789
First, he portrayed a "Goblin Bank Teller"
at the Gringotts Wizarding Bank.

00:01:09.789 --> 00:01:15.109
He also played Griphook, an extraordinarily
grumpy employee of Gringotts, but only in

00:01:15.109 --> 00:01:17.880
Harry Potter and the Deathly Hallows: Part
2.

00:01:18.320 --> 00:01:21.060
"You probably don't remember that you —"
"That I showed you to your vault the first

00:01:21.060 --> 00:01:22.040
time you came to Gringotts?

00:01:23.360 --> 00:01:25.840
Even amongst goblins, you're famous, Harry
Potter."

00:01:26.620 --> 00:01:31.439
The same character was originally played by
the late Verne Troyer in the Sorcerer's Stone,

00:01:31.440 --> 00:01:33.720
with Warwick's voice dubbing his performance.

00:01:34.540 --> 00:01:40.620
The late Kevin Peter Hall might be the most
famous actor of the 1980s who was recognized

00:01:40.620 --> 00:01:41.280
the least.

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:46.240
Because he was more than seven feet tall,
Hall found work mostly playing movie monsters,

00:01:46.240 --> 00:01:48.380
typically inside a heavy costume.

00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:53.619
One notable albeit short-lived exception was
his appearance in Misfits of Science, the

00:01:53.619 --> 00:01:57.310
mid-'80s NBC series about a group of superpowered
individuals.

00:01:57.310 --> 00:02:00.000
Hall played a really tall guy who can shrink.

00:02:00.200 --> 00:02:00.740
Go figure.

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:05.980
Anyway, Hall's affinity for the makeup chair
brought him some pretty memorable roles: he

00:02:05.991 --> 00:02:10.920
was Harry in Harry and the Hendersons as well
as the titular bloodthirsty alien hunting

00:02:10.920 --> 00:02:15.820
down future governors Arnold Schwarzenegger
and Jesse Ventura in Predator.

00:02:16.040 --> 00:02:21.290
The costume and makeup work on the reptilian
Predator were so good that few realize the

00:02:21.290 --> 00:02:25.900
helicopter pilot at the end of the movie was
also portrayed by Kevin Peter Hall.

00:02:26.240 --> 00:02:26.980
The more you know!

00:02:27.660 --> 00:02:31.940
It goes without saying that Mark Hamill's
fans absolutely love the guy…

00:02:32.140 --> 00:02:33.520
"Hello, everyone!"

00:02:36.180 --> 00:02:41.190
And despite a career that spans hundreds of
credits over nearly 40 years, most of that

00:02:41.190 --> 00:02:47.269
praise and affection comes primarily for two
iconic roles: Luke Skywalker in the Star Wars

00:02:47.269 --> 00:02:52.020
movies and the voice of the Joker in a number
of animated Batman projects.

00:02:52.220 --> 00:02:57.299
In the former, he's at the center of a timeless
story of heroes and villains; in the latter,

00:02:57.300 --> 00:03:01.340
he brings nuance and depth to what could be
a one-note bad guy.

00:03:01.520 --> 00:03:06.040
Acting in Star Wars and doing voice work are
two very different disciplines, and it turns

00:03:06.040 --> 00:03:10.200
out that Hamill has combined those two things
on more than one occasion.

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:15.501
In addition to portraying a grizzled Luke
Skywalker in 2017's The Last Jedi, Hamill

00:03:15.501 --> 00:03:18.140
voices a character named Dobbu Scay.

00:03:18.140 --> 00:03:22.860
That's the little alien gambler who mistakes
BB-8 for a slot machine in the Canto Bight

00:03:22.880 --> 00:03:23.380
casino.

00:03:24.080 --> 00:03:28.980
During an exciting action sequence in Ryan
Reynolds' second outing as everybody's favorite

00:03:28.989 --> 00:03:32.989
Merc with a Mouth, Deadpool finds himself
butting heads with time-traveling villain

00:03:32.989 --> 00:03:36.859
Cable in his quest to dispatch young mutant
Russell Collins.

00:03:36.860 --> 00:03:41.020
In the ensuing chaos, Collins sets free Juggernaut,
another mutant.

00:03:41.320 --> 00:03:43.159
A big mutant.

00:03:43.160 --> 00:03:45.989
A big, hulking, angry mutant.

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:48.020
"I'm gonna rip you in half now."

00:03:48.360 --> 00:03:50.620
"That is such a juggernaut thing to say."

00:03:52.400 --> 00:03:57.720
Juggernaut is such a massive, hulking presence
that no human actor could have convincingly

00:03:57.730 --> 00:04:03.069
portrayed the seemingly indestructible killing
machine, so he's a creation of some of the

00:04:03.069 --> 00:04:06.360
most advanced cinema CGI ever utilized.

00:04:06.480 --> 00:04:11.820
But his voice was provided by a real guy,
and it came courtesy of another actor who's

00:04:11.829 --> 00:04:18.450
used to acting in superhero action comedies
without showing his actual human face: Ryan

00:04:18.450 --> 00:04:19.140
Reynolds himself.

00:04:19.740 --> 00:04:25.320
After years of playing bit parts in a slew
of TV shows, Canadian actor Alain Chanoine

00:04:25.320 --> 00:04:29.110
was thrust into stardom with a major role
in Suicide Squad.

00:04:29.110 --> 00:04:34.160
He plays Incubus, one of the nastiest characters
in a movie chock full of them, and works alongside

00:04:34.160 --> 00:04:36.480
Cara Delevingne as Enchantress.

00:04:36.480 --> 00:04:41.460
He also has a second, bit part as one of the
Enchantress' Eyes of the Adversary, former

00:04:41.460 --> 00:04:44.860
human beings transformed into eyeball-covered
freaks.

00:04:44.860 --> 00:04:49.060
According to Chanoine, different people were
in charge of casting different parts of the

00:04:49.060 --> 00:04:52.200
movie, and he scored in auditions with both
groups.

00:04:52.920 --> 00:04:55.760
Wild Wild West isn't the best movie.

00:04:55.920 --> 00:04:59.600
In fact, let's not sugarcoat things, it's
just straight-up bad.

00:04:59.840 --> 00:05:03.720
It even won five Razzie Awards, including
Worst Picture.

00:05:03.720 --> 00:05:09.220
But it's a big, silly summer movie, featuring
Will Smith at the height of his '90s superstardom

00:05:09.230 --> 00:05:15.040
as charming Army Captain Jim West, and the
magnificent comic actor Kevin Kline as West's

00:05:15.040 --> 00:05:17.160
partner, marshal Artemus Gordon.

00:05:17.280 --> 00:05:23.780
Even with all that good guy star power, Kenneth
Branagh steals the movie as the evil Dr. Arliss

00:05:23.790 --> 00:05:29.910
Loveless, an over-the-top caricature of a
villain and a bitter, former Confederate scientist

00:05:29.910 --> 00:05:36.710
who takes his post-Civil War revenge by kidnapping
American president Ulysses S. Grant and holding

00:05:36.710 --> 00:05:40.280
him hostage aboard his giant, steampunk robot
spider.

00:05:40.360 --> 00:05:44.760
If the actor who portrays President Grant
looks familiar, he should, because he's in

00:05:44.760 --> 00:05:46.230
most of the rest of the movie.

00:05:46.230 --> 00:05:51.310
Under some identity-concealing prosthetics
and transformative makeup, that's Kevin Kline

00:05:51.310 --> 00:05:53.740
again, in all his presidential glory.

